avaiṣṇavo gurur na syād
vaiṣṇavaḥ śva-paco guruḥ\"}}]}],[\"$\",\"$L29\",\"child-499\",{\"child\":\"$23:props:children:0:props:children:props:page:child_items:4:children:4\",\"hasId\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"em-mb-4 em-leading-8 em-text-base s-justify\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"“A scholarly brāhmaṇa, expert in all subjects of Vedic knowledge, is unfit to become a spiritual master without being a Vaiṣṇava, or expert in the science of Kṛṣṇa consciousness. But a person born in a family of a lower caste can become a spiritual master if he is a Vaiṣṇava, or Kṛṣṇa conscious.” (Padma Purāṇa)\"}}]}],[\"$\",\"$L29\",\"child-500\",{\"child\":\"$23:props:children:0:props:children:props:page:child_items:4:children:5\",\"hasId\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"em-mb-4 em-leading-8 em-text-base s-justify\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"The problems of material existence – birth, old age, disease and death – cannot be counteracted by accumulation of wealth and economic development. In many parts of the world there are states which are replete with all facilities of life, which are full of wealth and economically developed, yet the problems of material existence are still present. They are seeking peace in different ways, but they can achieve real happiness only if they consult Kṛṣṇa, or the Bhagavad-gītā and Śrīmad-Bhāgavatam – which constitute the science of Kṛṣṇa – through the bona fide representative of Kṛṣṇa, the man in Kṛṣṇa consciousness.\"}}]}],\"$L35\",\"$L36\"]]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"37:[[\"$\",\"source\",null,{\"srcSet\":\"https://simpleanalyticsbadges.com/vedabase.io?mode=auto\",\"media\":\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"}],[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"src\":\"https://simpleanalyticsbadges.com/vedabase.io?mode=auto\",\"loading\":\"lazy\",\"referrerPolicy\":\"no-referrer\",\"crossOrigin\":\"anonymous\"}]]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"26:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"id\":\"footer\",\"className\":\"mt-auto w-full max-w-7xl 